menu "pico-e32"

config PICO_E32_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
    string "OTA manifest URL"
    default ""
    help
        Where Settings -> SYSTEM UPDATE looks for the update manifest, e.g.
        https://example.org/pico-e32.json  (see WC-4a in docs/firmware/pico-e32-wifi-networking.md
        for the JSON shape).

        Empty (the default) disables the check and the menu says so, so a build never silently
        points at someone else's endpoint.

        This is Kconfig rather than a -D define on purpose: a quoted string does not survive the
        make -> idf.py -> CMake -> compiler hop (the quotes are stripped and the macro ends up
        empty), whereas sdkconfig quotes it correctly.

endmenu
